From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:46:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate the UI to Jetpack Compose with Material 3 Expressive

Adds Jetpack Compose (UI 1.12.1, Material 3 1.5.0-rc01, graphics-shapes,
material-icons-extended, activity/lifecycle-compose) next to the existing View
UI, and moves the app's own screens to the Material 3 Expressive style of
m3.material.io: MaterialExpressiveTheme, the expressive MotionScheme, the
MaterialShapes shape set, wavy progress, morphing loading indicators, floating
toolbars, button groups, split buttons and toggle buttons.

The colour scheme is not redefined in Compose: GbColorScheme reads the theme
attributes the activity already applied, so the user's theme, accent colour,
AMOLED black, contrasting surfaces and dynamic colour carry over unchanged.
The Material 3 Expressive corner radii are also applied as a theme overlay in
ActivityTheme, which makes every remaining View screen rounder without touching
a layout.

Screens now drawn by Compose:
- the first run flow, previously an activity plus five fragments, a ViewPager2
  and a self-drawn page indicator: a HorizontalPager with a stretching page
  indicator, MaterialShapes heroes and an Expressive theme picker
- the navigation drawer, fed by R.menu.activity_main_drawer so every entry keeps
  its behaviour, dispatched through the same onNavigationItemSelected()
- the settings screen and, through AbstractPreferenceFragment, every settings
  sub-screen: the fragment keeps inflating its real preference XML and keeps its
  dialogs, listeners and search, while Compose walks the live tree and draws it.
  Rows show the value of each preference kind, disabled rows are not clickable,
  and screens whose widgets cannot be reproduced faithfully (device settings,
  drag-sortable loyalty cards, Garmin and Hybrid HR watchface settings) opt out
  and keep the View list.
- the backup-on-open settings, the About screen, and the sleep score details
  sheet, previously a BottomSheetDialog with a layout, now a Compose
  ModalBottomSheet with wavy score rings

The debug build type gets its own application id (.debug) and its own Pebble
content provider authority, so the debug build installs next to the production
app or a nightly without replacing it or touching its data.

New strings are English with Simplified and Traditional Chinese translations.

Also builds faster in mainland China: settings.gradle.kts puts the Aliyun and
Huawei mirrors in front of the official repositories (keeping the content
filters and FAIL_ON_PROJECT_REPOS), and the Gradle wrapper downloads from the
Tencent mirror, whose archive is byte-identical to the official one and is still
verified with the existing sha256.
